  Items discussed:question of the nite: should floating point be part of
        X3/J14, ADA vs IEEE fp,numerical analysis, Phil Koopman conference,
        porting Forth to a CRAY-2, Martin Tracy's wedding, Len Morgenstern's
        38th anniversary, Factoring O(N) for FFT, sines of sines ...

Minutes:
<H.SABBAGH> is here.
<[Gary] GARY-S>  any thoughts on tonite's question ?
<[Hadil] H.SABBAGH> Yes. Floating point should be part of the std.
<[Gary] GARY-S> thanks
<[Hadil] H.SABBAGH> what do you think?
<[Gary] GARY-S> any reason you feel that way ?
<[Hadil] H.SABBAGH> Well, I am a numerical analyist by training...
